-- title:
--   Taylor residual bound over the entire Gaussian fitted convex hull
-- statement:
--   For observations $x_1,\ldots,x_n\in\mathbb R^d$ and reference coordinates $v_{0i}$, define $a_i(\theta)=e^{\langle x_i,\theta\rangle-\|\theta\|^2/2}/v_{0i}-1$. Let $T_L(\theta)_i=e^{-\|\theta\|^2/2}\sum_{\ell=0}^L\langle x_i,\theta\rangle^\ell/(\ell!v_{0i})-1$, and let $V_L$ be the Gaussian Taylor subspace generated by the constant vector and the scaled coefficient vectors of the degree-$L$ Taylor polynomial. Let $K\subset\mathbb R^d$ be any set with $\|\theta\|\le S$ on $K$, where $T,S\ge0$. Assume $\|x_i\|\le T$ and $v_{0i}\ge e^{-(TS+S^2/2)}$ for all $i$. Put $\varepsilon_L=e^{2TS+S^2/2}(TS)^{L+1}/(L+1)!$. For every $u\in\operatorname{conv}\{a(\theta):\theta\in K\}$, $$\|u-P_{V_L}u\|_2\le\sqrt n\,\varepsilon_L.$$ Compactness or finiteness of $K$ is not required. This extends atomwise approximation to all fitted vectors in the convex hull.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianWidth.lean#L272-L301

